Pay attention kids.  Dave didn't slip up here.  Yes he could have gone
for a +3 Mojo, but once a weapon is at +6, it is in danger of evaporating
if enchanted further.  By asking for +2 Mojo, he can safely enchant it
to +8 with two blessed scrolls of enchant armor.  He is also more likely
to get the requested enchantment of +2 vs. +3.

BTW, this is less of an issue with swords.  If you are running around
with a +6 Excalibur, Frost Brand, Stormy, etc. and you get a hold of


.... Back to wands of wishing... Perhaps a WOW of when found should have
a probability of having been already charged once.  Right now, a WOW
will evaporate if charged more than once, so an adventurer risks a bit
by charging the wand.  Now granted, they will not try to charge it til
it's down to 0 wishes, but if we also limit even blessed scrolls of charging
to only recharging by one wish, then the nethacker risks losing his/her
"wrested" wish by attempting to get another via charging.

  It would also make sense to have the probability of the wand being
once-charged be higher for the early levels, where a player is "luckier"
(in a sense) to get one in the first place.  For that matter, such a
wand should also likely have fewer wishes in it. 
